.TH IAD\-DATE\-RANGE\-INPUT 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
date_range_input \- one entry for a date range (2026\-11\-02 \(en 2026\-11\-09) with the calendar in its left section, in a popover or a dialog, that selects the range; the sibling of DateInput the way RangeSlider is of scale
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
DateRangeInput::new(text: &'a str, view: Date, on_input: impl Fn(String) \-> M + 'a)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBDateRangeInput\fR: one entry for a date range (\fB2026\-11\-02 \(en 2026\-11\-09\fR) with the calendar in its left section, in a popover or a dialog, that selects the range; the sibling of \fBDateInput\fR the way \fBRangeSlider\fR is of \fBscale\fR.
.PP
The rule is \fBDateRange::pick\fR: the first click sets the start, the second the end (swapped when earlier), a third starts over. Everything is controlled like \fBDateInput\fR: you keep the text, the month on show and the \fBDateRange\fR (set the text from \fBDateRange::text\fR when a range is picked), and the widget reports \fBon_input(text)\fR, \fBon_pick(range)\fR, \fBon_view(first\-of\-month)\fR and, to preview the range under the pointer, \fBon_hover(day)\fR.
.PP
.nf
.RS
DateRangeInput::new(&self.text, self.view, Message::Text)
    .selected(self.range)
    .hover(self.hover)
    .on_pick(Message::Picked)
    .on_view(Message::View)
    .on_hover(Message::Hover)
.RE
.fi
.PP
An unparsable or out\-of\-range date, or an end before the start, draws the entry in its error state, once \fBrevealed\fR (pass the \fBField\fR's interaction inside a \fBField\fR); \fBvalidity\fR is the message for it.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.TP
.B DateRangeInput::new(text: &'a str, view: Date, on_input: impl Fn(String) \-> M + 'a)
\fBtext\fR is the entry's content (\fB2026\-11\-02 \(en 2026\-11\-09\fR, see \fBDateRange::parse\fR); \fBview\fR is any date in the month the calendar shows.
