.SH EVENTS
Callbacks that produce the application's message.
.TP
.B \&.on_pick(f: impl Fn(DateRange) \-> M + 'a)
A day was clicked: gets the new selection (\fBDateRange::pick\fR).
.TP
.B \&.on_view(f: impl Fn(Date) \-> M + 'a)
The previous / next month button was pressed; gets the first day of the new month. The month\-level compatibility path: called only while months show, and the title is not navigable. Use \fBon_nav\fR for the levels (it takes precedence).
.TP
.B \&.on_nav(f: impl Fn(CalendarView) \-> M + 'a)
The calendar moved (arrow, title, month or year cell, "Today"): gets the whole new \fBCalendarView\fR. Drilling down never changes the selection: days are picked only at the \fBMonth\fR level, so the range rule (\fBDateRange::pick\fR) is untouched by zooming.
.TP
